; A small original 6502 program, for proving compiled and interpreted
; execution agree with no game corpus present.
;
; ORIGINAL WORK. Nothing here comes from the game source. It exercises what the
; lowering must get right: straight-line work, a structured conditional, a
; structured loop, a call and return, and an interrupt handler that the
; interpreter finishes when a compiled routine yields to it.

	.INCLUDE hll

	.=0E000

; The main loop. Global, so the emitter can be asked for it, and re-entered
; every iteration because JMP returns control to its own entry address.
MAIN::	CLI
	JSR WORK
	JMP MAIN

; Straight-line work, a conditional, and a countdown loop.
WORK::	LDA I,05
	STA 0300
	TAX
	INX
	IFEQ SKIP
	INY
SKIP:	ENDIF
	LDX I,04
	BEGIN
TOP:	DEX
	NEEND TOP
	RTS

; The interrupt handler: acknowledge, pet the watchdog, return. Acknowledging
; matters -- a handler that skipped it would be re-entered the moment RTI
; restored I.
	.=0E100
ISR::	STA 09D80
	STA 09E00
	RTI

; Vectors.
	.=0FFFC
	.WORD MAIN
	.WORD ISR
